  <div class="slide caption-page" data-document-role="page" data-label="C12 - Caption (copy/paste)">
    <div class="caption-flag">Caption - not for posting</div>
    <div class="caption-body">Bright lights and a cluttered, busy room can wear a sensitive child down before anyone has said a word, and it comes down to brain load.<br><br>Vision feeds the same processing system as the other senses. For a child with visual over-responsivity, a busy, over-decorated, flickering space takes extra brain effort to process. It piles onto everything else their nervous system is already handling. The classroom that looks cheerful and stimulating to us can feel like constant visual static to them.<br><br>Often, less visual noise means more brain capacity left over for focus and staying regulated. A calmer space is not boring or under-stimulating. It is a genuine kindness to a sensitive system. Calm spaces are not boring. They are kind.</div>
