  <div class="slide caption-page" data-document-role="page" data-label="C13 - Caption (copy/paste)">
    <div class="caption-flag">Caption - not for posting</div>
    <div class="caption-body">Your sensitive child can come home wiped out from a day that looked completely ordinary from the outside, and the reason is real brain work.<br><br>Screening out background noise, tolerating scratchy clothes, reading a busy classroom, holding it together in a loud lunchroom, all of it draws on the brain's limited resources. And because a sensitive nervous system does less automatic filtering, that processing runs nearly nonstop all day long.<br><br>So by pickup, the tank is genuinely empty. The after-school collapse is not defiance or manipulation. It is depletion from hours of invisible effort you could not see happening. They did not have a hard day on paper. They had a hard day inside their brain. Tired from the inside out.</div>
