    <div class="caption-flag">Caption - not for posting</div>
    <div class="caption-body">Your sensitive child's brain picks up subtle details that most people filter right out. The tag, the hum, the flicker, the tiny shift in your expression.<br><br>Heightened sensitivity means the brain registers fine-grained information others miss, with greater activation in regions tied to awareness and depth of processing. That is exactly why sensitive kids can be so perceptive, so empathetic, so tuned in to how everyone around them is feeling.<br><br>It is also why the small stuff that other people tune out can pile up on them quickly. The gift and the challenge run on the very same wiring, just pointed in two directions. They notice everything, and that is the whole point of who they are.</div>
